WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.100
Monopoly

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:09.380
Why does MR lie below demand for a monopolist?

3
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:22.200
To sell one more unit it must cut price on every unit, so MR = the new unit’s price minus revenue lost on all previous ones. For a straight-line demand curve, MR has the same intercept and twice the slope.

4
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.510
The two-step move for monopoly price?

5
00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:36.050
Find Q where MR = MC, then go straight up to the demand curve to read the price. Setting price at the MR = MC intersection is the classic mistake.

6
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.580
What are the two kinds of barrier to entry?

7
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:49.790
Legal — patents, licences, government franchises. Natural — huge economies of scale, control of a key resource, network effects.

8
00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:55.070
Perfect price discrimination — the striking result?

9
00:00:55.070 --> 00:01:08.630
The firm produces the efficient quantity, so DWL = 0 — but CS = 0 and the firm captures the entire surplus. Efficient and not equitable: the cleanest proof that efficiency ≠ fairness.

10
00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:11.000
Monopoly — 4 cards
